<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Calchaquí Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1560–1667</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Calchaquí Wars were a series of risings by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diaguita">Diaguita</a> peoples of the Calchaquí valleys in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> against Spanish rule between 1560 and 1667. The largest, in 1630–1643 and 1658–1659, the latter led by the adventurer Pedro Bohórquez, who claimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> descent, were crushed, and the Spanish deported whole communities, including the Quilmes, far from their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/calchaqui-wars.jpg" alt="Calchaquí Wars" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cmglee and Cephas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patagonian_lang.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
